%% Zero-downtime change of the cells (stateless clusters): one cell at a time, its applications migrated out for a
%% cluster upgrade or rebuild, updated in place for a release, verified, then the next cell. Same pipeline in dev, acc, prd.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Pipeline<br/>(cluster upgrade or release)
    participant A as Cell az1
    participant B as Cell az2
    participant T as DNS<br/>(public and private zones)
    Note over A,B: Every app in its home cell,<br/>internal and external.<br/>Each cell can carry<br/>100 % (N+1).
    P->>B: Pre-scale: raise HPA minReplicas to full-load capacity,<br/>the cluster autoscaler adds nodes
    P->>A: Cluster upgrade: migrate az1's apps to az2 - deploy, test on the per-cell names, DNS switch<br/>(release: nothing moves, az1's apps update in place by their rolling update)
    T-->>A: The home routes leave az1: its records move to az2<br/>within a minute + TTL, connections drain
    P->>A: Upgrade the control plane and every<br/>node pool (surge), rebuild from IaC,<br/>or move the cell's branch
    A->>A: Flux reconciles every app,<br/>health checks
    P->>A: Smoke and synthetic tests through<br/>the per-cell test host names
    P->>T: Cluster upgrade: after soak, migrate az1's apps back
    Note over P,A: Watch the error-rate and latency SLOs.<br/>Breach: stop<br/>(release: move the branch back).
    P->>A: Release: soak, pre-scale az1,<br/>repeat steps 2-7 for az2 (and az3)<br/>Cluster update: az2 (and az3)<br/>follow later on the slow speed
    P->>B: Remove the pre-scale: HPA / KEDA and<br/>the cluster autoscaler take over
